    "report": {
      "title": "How the SEC's 2018 'funding secured' case affected Tesla's stock",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "executive_summary",
          "heading": "Executive summary",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "text": "On 27 September 2018 the SEC charged Elon Musk with securities fraud over his 7 August 2018 tweets about taking Tesla private, alleging that his claim that funding was secured was false and misleading. Two days later Musk and Tesla settled without admitting or denying the allegations, and the court entered a final judgment on 16 October 2018.",
              "source_ids": [
                "sec_charges",
                "sec_settlement",
                "sec_lr_24413"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Tesla's shares returned {{calc:ret_sec_charges}} across the SEC's charges and {{calc:ret_settlement}} across the settlement, measured from the last close before each event to the first close after it.",
              "source_ids": [
                "src_prices",
                "fortune_2018_09_28",
                "fortune_2018_10_01"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "case_overview",
          "heading": "Case overview",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "text": "The SEC's complaint, filed in federal court in Manhattan, alleged that when Musk tweeted that funding was secured he had not discussed or confirmed key deal terms, including price, with any potential funding source. These are the SEC's allegations: the case was settled rather than tried, so no court ruled on whether they were true.",
              "source_ids": [
                "complaint",
                "sec_charges"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Musk called the SEC's action unjustified and said he had always acted in the best interests of investors.",
              "source_ids": [
                "fortune_2018_09_28",
                "techcrunch_2018_09_27"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "legal_developments",
          "heading": "Legal developments",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "text": "Under the settlement announced on 29 September 2018, Musk and Tesla each agreed to pay a civil penalty, Musk agreed to step down as Tesla's chairman in favour of an independent chairman, and Tesla agreed to appoint two new independent directors.",
              "source_ids": [
                "sec_settlement"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "The court approved the settlement and entered its final judgment on 16 October 2018.",
              "source_ids": [
                "sec_lr_24413",
                "techcrunch_2018_10_16"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "market_reaction",
          "heading": "Market reaction",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "text": "Shares returned {{calc:ret_tweet}} across the 'funding secured' tweet itself.",
              "source_ids": [
                "src_prices"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "They returned {{calc:ret_sec_charges}} from the close before the charges to the close after them. Fortune reported that investors feared the lawsuit could lead to Musk being ousted as chief executive.",
              "source_ids": [
                "src_prices",
                "fortune_2018_09_28"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "After the settlement they returned {{calc:ret_settlement}}, which Fortune and TechCrunch reported as recovering the previous week's losses. Across the court's approval they returned {{calc:ret_court_approval}}.",
              "source_ids": [
                "src_prices",
                "fortune_2018_10_01",
                "techcrunch_2018_10_01",
                "techcrunch_2018_10_16"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Over the whole period shown, from early July to the end of October 2018, shares returned {{calc:ret_period}}.",
              "source_ids": [
                "src_prices"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
